# Lane SIGNKMS-1: the Ed25519 public keys an OpenBFME release may be signed with (docs/RELEASE.md, "Release signing").
#
# One key per line: <64 lower-case hex digits of the public key>  <label>     ('#' starts a comment line; blank lines are allowed)
# Rules (checked by tools/release/release_keys.py, the launcher's build_info.json and the packagers): 1 to 8 keys, no key twice, labels
# [a-z0-9-]{1,32}; the FIRST entry is launcher/release_key.pub, the legacy key every launcher made before this list trusts.
# The packagers compile this list into the launcher (build_info.json "release_keys") and the game (release_trust.gd RELEASE_KEYS); a
# signature is valid when it verifies under ANY key here, raw (scheme v1) or over the signature envelope (scheme v2).
# Lane RELGH-3: stable-2026 is the stable Actions key. Its private half lives only in the GitHub environment `stable-signing` (the owner's
# review approves every use: tools/release/stable_environment.json) and an offline encrypted backup. deck-2026 stays offline, never in CI or
# GitHub: it is the recovery key that can ship a launcher without stable-2026 (docs/RELEASE.md, "Stable signing on GitHub Actions").
53530cc89e5e56b1b8e721e3b23abc0aca3f82397543e256c2d4a7c4255d27c9  deck-2026
464d22a1b0929456f3d90a73965ad1bff7536613a6ddfe77041b1607fce50fe5  stable-2026
